{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 19, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "Hark! Pray lend thine ears to this most wondrous itinerary for thy voyage to the fabled isle of Japan.\n\n**First Day: Arriveth in Tokyo the Mighty**\nUpon thy arrival at Narita’s gates descendeth thou into the bustling metropolis of Tokyo the radiant. Seek forthwith the ancient streets of Asakusa where the great Senso-ji Temple doth stand in solemn grandeur. Offer thy respects to the deities and partake of a steaming bowl of ramen in a humble eatery nearby. As the sun doth dip below the horizon retire to the neon-lit district of Shinjuku where thou shalt find lodging fit for a king or perhaps a humble ryokan for a taste of tradition.\n\n**Second Day: The Gardens of Edo and the Theatres of Old**\nAwake at dawn and venture unto the Imperial Gardens where the cherry blossoms may yet linger if fortune favors thee. Walk the paths trod by shoguns of yore and breathe deep the scented air. In the afternoon hie thee to the Kabuki-za Theatre where the art of drama doth unfold in vivid splendor. Marvel at the painted faces and the graceful movements of the players. As night falleth sup upon delicate sushi in the Tsukiji Outer Market ere thou returnest to thy lodgings.\n\n**Third Day: The Frozen Peaks of Hakone**\nFlee the clamor of the city and journey to Hakone the misty where the great Mount Fuji doth watch o’er the land. Ride the cable car unto the volcanic valleys and bathe thy weary bones in the healing waters of an onsen. Feast upon black eggs boiled in sulfur’s embrace that granteth seven years of fortune. As evening draweth nigh retire to a ryokan where tatami mats and futons await thee and dream of the gods.\n\n**Fourth Day: The Imperial Splendor of Kyoto**\nBy swift train hasten to Kyoto the ancient where emperors once ruled and temples stand as testaments to time’s passage. Visit the Kinkaku-ji the Golden Pavilion that gleameth in the sun’s embrace. Walk the philosopher’s path by the canal where the cherry trees whisper secrets of the past. In the evening don thy finest robes and attend a tea ceremony where the matcha’s bitterness yieldeth to sweet harmony. Sup upon kaiseki a feast fit for the heavens.\n\n**Fifth Day: The Sacred Trails of Nara**\nUpon the morrow journey to Nara the gentle where the sacred deer do roam freely and bow to thy gentle hand. Visit the Todai-ji where the great Buddha doth sit in silent judgment. Climb the steps of the Kasuga Taisha where lanterns of stone and bronze guard ancient paths. Partake of kakinoha-zushi a delicacy wrapped in persimmon leaves and drink deeply of sake blessed by the gods.\n\n**Sixth Day: The Coastal Wonders of Osaka**\nHie thee to Osaka the bountiful where the castle of the shogun standeth proud albeit not so grand as once it was. Wander the Dotonbori streets where lights dance upon the waters and takoyaki doth tempt thy palate. Ascend the Umeda Sky Building and gaze upon the city as a god might. In the night partake of okonomiyaki a savory pancake prepared before thine eyes.\n\n**Seventh Day: The Farewell Supper and Flight Home**\nOn the final morn revisit thy favorite haunts in Tokyo to purchase trinkets and treasures to bring back to thy homeland. Feast one last time upon wagyu beef so tender it melteth in thy mouth and wash it down with a cup of green tea. As thou boardest the plane that shall bear thee hence bid adieu to the land of the rising sun with a heart full of memories and a soul enriched by the journey’s splendor.\n\nThus endeth thy grand adventure in Japan. May the gods smile upon thy travels and bring thee safely home.", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -1.7175990343093872}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.0001573438785271719}, {"token": "!", "logprob": -0.339164674282074}, {"token": " P", "logprob": -0.6619545221328735}, {"token": "ray", "logprob": -0.001546973828226328}, {"token": " lend", "logprob": -0.7208727598190308}, {"token